# Direct runtime dependencies of the MattStash API server (human-edited version ranges).
#
# This file is the INPUT to the hash-pinned lock (requirements.lock), which is what the
# Docker images and CI actually install. See the header of requirements.lock for the exact
# regeneration command.
#
# * mattstash itself is deliberately NOT listed here. The images install it from this
#   repository (`pip install .`), so an image always contains the library of its own commit.
#   The library's runtime dependencies (pykeepass, httpx, ...) are pulled into the lock
#   from the root pyproject.toml when it is compiled together with this file.
# * Test/lint tooling lives in requirements-dev.txt and is never installed in the image.
